Game of Life on sparse tiles run by several places with a directory
(benchmarks/life/life-places.m), its places spawned at the host: each
place steps its own tiles and reads its neighbours' borders from halos, and
the directory decides every tile's fate and moves tiles from a place with
more than its share to one with fewer. The population, checksum and
active tiles are life-sparse.m's for the same world, for any number of
places (life-sparse.test), as Life is exact: the worlds cover tiles of 4 to
64 cells, soups from none to the whole world, a side that is not a power of
two, gliders that reach the world's edge, and a place's pool running out.

Sequential, at -O0 and -O2, and with the loops on the host's threads at -O2.
The -O0 build has no --offload-arch, as life-sparse.test's has none.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-registered-target, libomp
RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-places.m -o %t0
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx1030 %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-places.m -o %t2
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx1030 %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-places.m -o %t.omp

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=A,A2
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=1 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A1
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=A,A2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=A,A3
A1: Game of Life, Mercury, GPU processes, sparse tiles, 1 places
A: Game of Life, Mercury, GPU processes, sparse tiles, {{[23]}} places
A-NEXT: World: 256 x 256 cells, tiles of 16 x 16, 256 in each place's pool
A-NEXT: Soup: 64 x 64 cells at the centre
A-NEXT: Steps: 50
A-NEXT: Population: 562
A-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end
A2-NEXT: Tiles moved: 3
A3-NEXT: Tiles moved: 13
A1: Population: 562
A1-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A1-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end
A1-NEXT: Tiles moved: 0

Every allocation collects, at -O2, where LLVM keeps pointers into arrays
across a collection (design document, "Roots that only the optimizer
makes").
RUN: %libomp-env MERK_GC_EVERY_ALLOC=1 LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A

Gliders that reach the edge make tiles start and end throughout, so tiles
move all the time; the moves are the same in every run, as the directory
chooses them by position. LIFE_MOVES=0 keeps the owners fixed.
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,EDGE2
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,EDGE4
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=7 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,EDGE7
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,EDGE4
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_MOVES=0 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,FIXED
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_MOVES=1 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=EDGE,ONE
EDGE: Population: 747
EDGE-NEXT: Checksum: 7031763
EDGE-NEXT: Active tiles: 182 at most, 165 at the end
EDGE2-NEXT: Tiles moved: 509
EDGE4-NEXT: Tiles moved: 710
EDGE7-NEXT: Tiles moved: 734
FIXED-NEXT: Tiles moved: 0
ONE-NEXT: Tiles moved: 609

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
ODD: Population: 157
ODD-NEXT: Checksum: 2963654

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=100 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE
WHOLE: Population: 4947
WHOLE-NEXT: Checksum: 158368224
WHOLE-NEXT: Active tiles: 1024 at most, 856 at the end
WHOLE-NEXT: Tiles moved: 143

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_WORLD=64 LIFE_TILE=4 LIFE_SOUP=30 LIFE_STEPS=1000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
SMALL: Population: 34
SMALL-NEXT: Checksum: 82077

RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=512 LIFE_TILE=64 LIFE_SOUP=128 LIFE_STEPS=400 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WIDE
WIDE: Population: 1899
WIDE-NEXT: Checksum: 265191136

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=0 LIFE_STEPS=10 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EMPTY
EMPTY: Population: 0
EMPTY-NEXT: Checksum: 0
EMPTY-NEXT: Active tiles: 0 at most, 0 at the end

A place's pool runs out: the program says so and ends with status 1, as
the places end.
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=10 LIFE_CAPACITY=100 not %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
FULL: A place's pool ran out of tiles: raise LIFE_CAPACITY.

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_PLACES=33 not %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USAGE
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_MOVES=-1 not %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USAGE
USAGE: LIFE_TILE must be a power of two of at least 4 that divides LIFE_WORLD, with fewer than 2^21 tiles, LIFE_SOUP from 0 to LIFE_WORLD, LIFE_STEPS at least 2, LIFE_CAPACITY at least 2, LIFE_PLACES from 1 to 32, and LIFE_MOVES at least 0.
